---
layout: base.njk
theme: theme-dark
bodyClass: home
statement: An agent runs code it wrote a minute ago and reads whatever the web hands it. backfabric assumes it will misbehave one day, and limits what it can reach and what it can hide.
preload:
  - sky
  - city
---
{% from "art.njk" import layer %}
<section class="hero" data-scene aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="scene scene-back" aria-hidden="true">
    {{ layer(scene.sky, "art art-sky") }}
    {{ layer(scene.city, "art art-city") }}
  </div>
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <p class="kicker"><i aria-hidden="true"></i> Open source · NixOS · MIT</p>
    <h1 id="hero-title" class="wordmark">backfabric</h1>
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="pitch">Run AI agents on servers you own.</p>
      <p class="lede">backfabric turns Hetzner bare metal into an encrypted, locked-down Kubernetes cluster: agents run in sandboxes, nothing in it can be reached from the internet, and every request to its API is logged. All of it is NixOS code you can read.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn btn-sun" href="#start">Get started</a>
        <a class="btn btn-glass" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {# In front of the wordmark, behind the words. #}
  <div class="scene scene-front" aria-hidden="true">
    {{ layer(scene.palmA, "palm palm-a") }}
    {{ layer(scene.palmB, "palm palm-b") }}
    {{ layer(scene.thicket, "thicket thicket-left") }}
    {{ layer(scene.thicket, "thicket thicket-right") }}
  </div>
  <p class="facts">
    <span><b>{{ status.shipped.length }}</b>shipped</span>
    <span><b>{{ status.inProgress.length }}</b>in review</span>
    <span><b>{{ status.planned.length }}</b>planned</span>
    <span><b>{{ repo.adrs.length }}</b>decision records</span>
  </p>
</section>

<div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="marquee-track">
    {% for i in [1, 2] %}<span>LUKS</span><b>✦</b><span>btrfs raid1</span><b>✦</b><span>unlock over SSH</span><b>✦</b><span>k3s</span><b>✦</b><span>CIS hardened</span><b>✦</b><span>OpenBao</span><b>✦</b><span>OpenTelemetry</span><b>✦</b><span>Agent Substrate</span><b>✦</b><span>gVisor</span><b>✦</b><span>PostgreSQL</span><b>✦</b>{% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>

<div class="sheet">
<section id="why" class="section aura" aria-labelledby="why-title">
  <div class="section-head">
    <p class="eyebrow"><b>01</b> Why</p>
    <h2 id="why-title" class="display reveal">Agents are software<br>you <span class="sun">can't fully trust</span>.</h2>
    <p class="manifesto" data-read>{% for word in statement.split(" ") %}<span style="--i: {{ loop.index0 }}">{{ word }}</span> {% endfor %}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bento">
    <article class="card wide reveal" data-glow style="--tint: var(--amber); --glow: rgb(255 194 102 / 0.16)">
      <div class="viz nest" aria-hidden="true">host<div>cluster<div>gVisor sandbox<div class="agent">agent</div></div></div></div>
      <p class="card-tag">Sandbox</p>
      <h3>One sandbox per agent</h3>
      <p>Each agent runs in its own gVisor sandbox, not directly on the server's kernel. Between tasks it is frozen to a snapshot; the next request resumes it with its memory and files.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card narrow reveal" data-glow style="--tint: var(--teal); --glow: rgb(47 243 224 / 0.14)">
      <div class="viz" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ports">{% for n in range(0, 48) %}<i{% if n == 29 %} class="open"{% endif %}></i>{% endfor %}</div>
        <p class="viz-note"><span>inbound ports</span><b>1 open: ssh, keys only</b></p>
      </div>
      <p class="card-tag">Network</p>
      <h3>Nothing answers from outside</h3>
      <p>From the internet a host answers on one port: SSH, with keys only. Nothing in the cluster, its API included, can be reached from outside the host.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card narrow reveal" data-glow style="--tint: var(--pink); --glow: rgb(255 46 136 / 0.16)">
      <div class="viz disks" aria-hidden="true">
        <div><span>disk 1</span><b>LUKS · locked</b></div>
        <div><span>disk 2 · mirror</span><b>LUKS · locked</b></div>
        <div class="key"><span>passphrase over ssh</span><b>••••••••</b></div>
      </div>
      <p class="card-tag">Disks</p>
      <h3>Encrypted, unlocked by you</h3>
      <p>The disks are encrypted. After every reboot the server waits until you send the passphrase over SSH. It is kept in your password manager, not on the server and not in git.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card wide reveal" data-glow style="--tint: var(--violet); --glow: rgb(138 92 255 / 0.2)">
      <div class="viz log" aria-hidden="true">
        <ol>
          {%- for i in [1, 2] %}
          <li><span class="t">09:14:02</span><span class="who">api</span><span>get pods · sa/agent-7</span><span class="ok">allow</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">09:14:02</span><span class="who">openbao</span><span>read secret/agents/7</span><span class="ok">allow</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">09:14:03</span><span class="who">api</span><span>create service · NodePort</span><span class="no">deny</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">09:14:05</span><span class="who">otel</span><span>span task.run · ns/agents</span><span class="ok">verified</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">09:14:09</span><span class="who">api</span><span>create pod · image unpinned</span><span class="no">deny</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">09:14:11</span><span class="who">openbao</span><span>read secret/platform</span><span class="no">deny</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">09:14:12</span><span class="who">api</span><span>list secrets · sa/agent-7</span><span class="no">deny</span></li>
          <li><span class="t">09:14:15</span><span class="who">otel</span><span>log agent.stdout · ns/agents</span><span class="ok">verified</span></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ol>
      </div>
      <p class="card-tag">Audit</p>
      <h3>A record agents can't rewrite</h3>
      <p>Every request to the Kubernetes API and to the secret store is logged. What pods report goes to a collector on the host, outside the cluster, which notes who really sent it.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="what" class="section aura" style="--aura: rgb(47 243 224 / 0.1); --aura-x: -10%" aria-labelledby="what-title">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow"><b>02</b> What it is</p>
    <h2 id="what-title" class="display">Not a service.<br><span class="sea">Code you can read.</span></h2>
    <p class="intro">backfabric is the code that sets up servers you rent. It comes in three parts.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bento">
    <article class="card third reveal" data-glow>
      <pre class="snippet" aria-hidden="true"><span class="c"># hosts/node1/default.nix</span>
<span class="k">backfabric.disks</span>.devices = [
  <span class="s">"/dev/disk/by-id/nvme-..."</span>
  <span class="s">"/dev/disk/by-id/nvme-..."</span>
];
<span class="k">backfabric.network</span>.ipv4 = {
  address = <span class="s">"203.0.113.10"</span>;
  gateway = <span class="s">"203.0.113.1"</span>;
};
<span class="k">backfabric.access</span>.ssh.port = <span class="p">2222</span>;</pre>
      <p class="card-tag">nixosModules</p>
      <h3>The modules</h3>
      <p>NixOS modules that configure a server from the disks up. You enable them and set a handful of options. Nine so far: <code>disks</code>, <code>network</code>, <code>access</code>, <code>secrets</code>, <code>k3s</code>, <code>openbao</code>, <code>otel</code>, <code>substrate</code>, <code>postgres</code>.</p>
      <a class="more" href="/docs/overview/">What each one does <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="card third reveal" data-glow style="--glow: rgb(255 194 102 / 0.16)">
      <ol class="flow" aria-hidden="true"><li>sops init</li><li>keygen</li><li>sops add-host</li><li>probe</li><li>install</li><li>unlock</li><li>finalize</li><li>deploy</li></ol>
      <p class="card-tag">backfabric</p>
      <h3>The command</h3>
      <p><code>backfabric</code> takes a freshly rented server to a running host and keeps it up to date: it generates keys, inspects the hardware, installs, unlocks the disks after a reboot and deploys your changes. Each step can be run again after a failure and prints the next one.</p>
      <a class="more" href="/docs/fleet-shell/">Installing a host <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </article>
    <article class="card third reveal" data-glow style="--glow: rgb(47 243 224 / 0.14)">
      <pre class="snippet" aria-hidden="true"><span class="k">fleet/</span>                <span class="c"># private</span>
├─ flake.nix
├─ .sops.yaml
├─ <span class="k">hosts/</span>node1/
│  ├─ default.nix
│  ├─ facter.json
│  └─ <span class="s">*.pub</span>
└─ <span class="k">secrets/</span>
   └─ common.yaml      <span class="c"># encrypted</span></pre>
      <p class="card-tag">templates.default</p>
      <h3>Your private repository</h3>
      <p>The addresses, disk ids and encrypted secrets of your servers live in a private repository that you create from a template. The public code never contains them, and you decide when to update NixOS.</p>
      <a class="more" href="/docs/template/">The template <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="stack" class="section aura" style="--aura: rgb(138 92 255 / 0.2); --aura-x: 0%; --aura-y: 30%" aria-labelledby="stack-title">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow"><b>03</b> The stack</p>
    <h2 id="stack-title" class="display">Five layers.<br><span class="sun">One flake.</span></h2>
    <p class="intro">Each layer rests on the one below. The first four are on main, each with the records of its decisions; the task layer is in review.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="stack-grid">
    <div class="tower" data-tower data-active="1" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="plate dashed" style="--i: 4; --c: var(--coral)">Tasks</div>
      <div class="plate" style="--i: 3; --c: var(--pink)">Agents</div>
      <div class="plate" style="--i: 2; --c: var(--amber)">Secrets · Telemetry</div>
      <div class="plate" style="--i: 1; --c: var(--violet)">Cluster</div>
      <div class="plate" style="--i: 0; --c: var(--teal)">Host</div>
    </div>
    <ol class="layers">
      <li class="layer is-active" data-layer-text="1" style="--c: var(--teal)">
        <p class="layer-no" aria-hidden="true">01</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Host <span class="badge badge-ok">shipped</span></h3>
          <p>A rented Hetzner server becomes a NixOS host that can be rebuilt from code. Its disks are encrypted, and mirrored when there are two or more. After every boot it waits for your passphrase, sent over SSH. The only way in from outside is SSH with your key.</p>
          <p class="chips"><span>LUKS</span><span>btrfs raid1</span><span>unlock over SSH</span><span>nftables</span><span>IPv4 only</span></p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="layer" data-layer-text="2" style="--c: var(--violet)">
        <p class="layer-no" aria-hidden="true">02</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Cluster <span class="badge badge-ok">shipped</span></h3>
          <p>Kubernetes, as k3s, configured the way the K3s CIS hardening guide asks. Pods run under the strictest Pod Security level; the few namespaces that cannot are limited to images pinned by digest. Every API request is logged, Secrets are encrypted in the database, and a Service cannot be exposed outside the host. One server for now: joining more is not built yet.</p>
          <p class="chips"><span>k3s 1.36</span><span>embedded etcd</span><span>CIS guide</span><span>flannel</span><span>NetworkPolicy</span></p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="layer" data-layer-text="3" style="--c: var(--amber)">
        <p class="layer-no" aria-hidden="true">03</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Secrets &amp; telemetry <span class="badge badge-ok">shipped</span></h3>
          <p>Two services run on the host, beside the cluster rather than inside it, so they work even when the cluster does not. OpenBao keeps the secrets that workloads need and logs every access. An OpenTelemetry Collector takes what pods report, checks who sent it, and appends it to an archive on the host. The host's own secrets sit encrypted in your repository, and the host decrypts them with its SSH key.</p>
          <p class="chips"><span>OpenBao</span><span>OTel Collector</span><span>sops-nix</span><span>TLS only</span></p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="layer" data-layer-text="4" style="--c: var(--pink)">
        <p class="layer-no" aria-hidden="true">04</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Agent runtime <span class="badge badge-ok">shipped</span></h3>
          <p>Agent Substrate runs each agent as a long-lived actor in a gVisor sandbox: frozen to a snapshot between tasks, resumed on the next request. The agent itself is a container image built by Nix, Codex behind an A2A supervisor, published with build provenance. It reaches the OpenAI API with a placeholder key that the egress gateway replaces, so no credential enters the sandbox. The runtime is off until you enable it.</p>
          <p class="chips"><span>Agent Substrate</span><span>gVisor</span><span>Nix-built image</span><span>SLSA provenance</span></p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="layer" data-layer-text="5" style="--c: var(--coral)">
        <p class="layer-no" aria-hidden="true">05</p>
        <div>
          <h3>Task layer <span class="badge badge-wip">in review</span></h3>
          <p>The front door: a dispatcher that accepts tasks for agents over the A2A protocol, queues them with Hatchet and hands each to its agent. The PostgreSQL it keeps its records in is on main. Its design, the queue and A2A in the agent image are in review; the dispatcher itself, a Go service, is not written yet.</p>
          <p class="chips"><span>A2A</span><span>Hatchet</span><span>Go</span><span>PostgreSQL</span></p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="status" class="section" aria-labelledby="status-title">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow"><b>04</b> Status</p>
    <h2 id="status-title" class="display">Not finished,<br><span class="sea">and it says so.</span></h2>
    <p class="intro">A cluster has one server today, and nothing rolls a host back automatically after a bad change. Below: what is on main, what is in review, and what is decided but not built.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="meter reveal" aria-hidden="true">
    <i style="--n: {{ status.shipped.length }}; --c: var(--teal)"></i>
    <i style="--n: {{ status.inProgress.length }}; --c: var(--amber)"></i>
    <i style="--n: {{ status.planned.length }}; --c: var(--violet)"></i>
  </div>
  <div class="board">
    {% for col in [
      { title: "Shipped", cls: "full", colour: "var(--teal)", items: status.shipped },
      { title: "In review", cls: "", colour: "var(--amber)", items: status.inProgress },
      { title: "Planned", cls: "", colour: "var(--violet)", items: status.planned }
    ] %}
    <div class="column {{ col.cls }} reveal" style="--c: {{ col.colour }}">
      <h3>{{ col.title }} <span>{{ col.items.length }}</span></h3>
      <ul>
        {% for item in col.items %}
        <li>
          <p class="item-title">{{ item.title }}</p>
          <p class="item-text">{{ item.text }}</p>
          <p class="item-links">{% for link in item.links %}<a href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</p>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="start" class="section aura" style="--aura: rgb(255 107 74 / 0.14); --aura-x: 55%; --aura-y: 20%" aria-labelledby="start-title">
  <div class="start-grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow"><b>05</b> Get started</p>
      <h2 id="start-title" class="display">Install your<br><span class="sun">first host.</span></h2>
      <p class="intro">You need a Hetzner dedicated server, Nix on your own machine, an SSH key and a key for sops. Create your private repository from the template; its README explains every step below.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><span><code>backfabric keygen</code> creates the server's host keys and disk passphrase, on your machine</span></li>
        <li><span><code>backfabric sops add-host</code> lets the server decrypt its secrets</span></li>
        <li><span><code>backfabric probe</code> boots the installer on the server and records its hardware</span></li>
        <li><span><code>backfabric install</code> erases the disks, encrypts them and installs NixOS</span></li>
        <li><span><code>backfabric unlock</code> sends the passphrase so the server can boot</span></li>
        <li><span><code>backfabric finalize</code> deletes the local keys once the passphrase is in your password manager</span></li>
        <li><span><code>backfabric deploy</code> applies each later change you commit</span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn btn-sun" href="/docs/template/">The full walkthrough</a>
        <a class="btn btn-glass" href="/docs/fleet-shell/">How installing works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="terminal reveal" data-typed role="group" aria-label="Commands to create the private repository">
      <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>~/fleet</span></div>
      <pre><span data-line class="c"># a new private repository</span><span data-line><span class="p">$</span> <span data-cmd>mkdir fleet &amp;&amp; cd fleet</span></span><span data-line><span class="p">$</span> <span data-cmd>nix flake init -t github:backfabric/infra</span></span><span data-line><span class="p">$</span> <span data-cmd>git init &amp;&amp; git add -A</span></span><span data-line><span class="p">$</span> <span data-cmd>git commit -m "chore: initial fleet repository"</span></span><span data-line>&nbsp;</span><span data-line class="c"># the dev shell, then your sops key</span><span data-line><span class="p">$</span> <span data-cmd>direnv allow</span>   <span class="c"># or: nix develop</span></span><span data-line><span class="p">$</span> <span data-cmd>backfabric sops init --age age1...</span></span></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="principles" class="section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow"><b>06</b> How it is built</p>
    <h2 id="principles-title" class="display">Four rules<br>behind <span class="sun">the code</span>.</h2>
    <p class="intro">The full set, for people and coding agents alike, is in <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/AGENTS.md"><code>AGENTS.md</code></a>.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="rules reveal">
    <li><i class="sun" aria-hidden="true">i</i><h3>Upstream first</h3><p>NixOS's own options and established tools come before code of our own. Less custom code means less to audit.</p></li>
    <li><i class="sun" aria-hidden="true">ii</i><h3>Built from code</h3><p>Every host, every Kubernetes manifest and the agent image are built by Nix from pinned inputs. The same commit gives the same system.</p></li>
    <li><i class="sun" aria-hidden="true">iii</i><h3>Decisions on record</h3><p>Every choice that is hard to reverse has a short <a href="/docs/#decisions">decision record</a>: what was decided, and which options lost.</p></li>
    <li><i class="sun" aria-hidden="true">iv</i><h3>Tested on real servers</h3><p>CI checks that everything evaluates, and builds the agent image and this site. Whether a host boots and behaves is checked on real Hetzner machines, not in mocks. <a href="/docs/adr/0015-ci-evaluation-only/">ADR 0015</a></p></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="finale" aria-labelledby="finale-title">
  <div class="scene scene-back" aria-hidden="true">
    {{ layer(scene.sky, "art", true) }}
    {{ layer(scene.city, "art", true) }}
    {{ layer(scene.palmC, "palm palm-c", true) }}
    {{ layer(scene.palmA, "palm palm-a", true) }}
    {{ layer(scene.palmB, "palm palm-b", true) }}
    {{ layer(scene.thicket, "thicket thicket-left", true) }}
    {{ layer(scene.thicket, "thicket thicket-right", true) }}
  </div>
  <div class="finale-inner">
    <h2 id="finale-title" class="display reveal">Bare metal by day.<br><span class="sun">Agents by night.</span></h2>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn btn-sun" href="{{ site.repo }}">backfabric/infra on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="btn btn-glass" href="/docs/#decisions">{{ repo.adrs.length }} decision records</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</div>
